# Tauri config & capabilities

- Keep the CSP strict. Do not add remote origins to `connect-src` / `img-src` /
  `script-src`; all backend calls go over IPC.
- `externalBin` lists sidecars by base name (`binaries/tor`, `binaries/sing-box`,
  `binaries/lyrebird`, `binaries/obfs4proxy`); Tauri appends the
  `-<target-triple>` suffix. Keep this list in sync with how
  `scripts/download-deps.sh` stages sidecars.
- The updater `pubkey` is the trust root. Do not rotate it casually — changing it
  breaks updates for already-installed clients. The matching private key lives
  outside the repo (see `.github/RELEASE_SECRETS.md`).
- Grant the **minimum** capabilities in `capabilities/`. Do not add broad shell,
  fs, or http permissions.
